  "title_en": "Ramayana: The Epic of Rama in Meitei Tradition",
  "author": "Angom Gopi (adapted from Valmiki and Krittivasi Ramayana into 18th-century Manipuri Meiteilon)",
  "language": "Meitei (Manipuri)",
  "script": "Meitei Mayek",
  "genre": "Sacred Hindu Epic / Classical Meitei Translation & Narrative",
  "description": "The sacred Hindu epic Ramayana rendered into classical Meitei (Manipuri) literature. Adapted into Manipuri during the 18th-century royal court of King Garibniwaz (Pamheiba) by court poet Angom Gopi, the epic recounts the righteousness of Prince Rama of Ayodhya, his devoted wife Sita, his brother Lakshmana, their fourteen-year forest exile, the abduction of Sita by King Ravana of Lanka, the valor of Hanuman, and the eternal victory of Dharma over Adharma. The epic has been passed down across generations through the oral reciting tradition of Wari Leeba.",
  "source": "Manipuri Ramayana Manuscripts (Angom Gopi traditions), Wari Leeba oral narration archives, & Manipuri Sahitya Parishad",
  "copyright": "Public Domain (Classical 18th-century Meitei Literary Adaptation and Sacred Heritage)",
